# Make a Kysul follower through the wizard menu and dump every page of the
# character sheet, so the page holding "Innate Spells" is in a dump. Read by
# tools/check_kysul_nightmare.sh, bd inc-pu6v.282.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/runs/kn2 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/kysul-nightmare.keys 1
#
# THE DEFECT THIS OBSERVES. Kysul's rank-6 grant in lib/religion.irh read
#   Ability[CA_INNATE_SPELL,$"Nightmare"]
# but $"name" is resolved by Module::FindResource (src/Res.cpp), which matches
# the FULL name case-insensitively and searches monsters before spells. The
# monster "nightmare" (lib/mon4.irh) matched first, so Player::GainAbility's
# CA_INNATE_SPELL case took -1 from SpellNum() and granted nothing. The grant
# must name the spell's full resource name: $"Nightmare;spell"
# (lib/wspells.irh). The fix is already in lib/religion.irh; this script
# photographs the character sheet that proves it.
#
# WHY "Become Divine Champion" IS ENOUGH. It sets SacVals[god][8] = 30000 and
# calls gainedFavour ten times (src/Debug.cpp). gainedFavour (src/Prayer.cpp)
# raises the god level one rung per call while the raw favour exceeds the
# next FAVOUR_CHART rung (lib/religion.irh: Kysul's are 300, 750, 1500, 3000,
# 12000, 24000, 48000, 64000, 96000, 128000). 30000 clears the first six
# rungs and stops at the 48000 rung, so the character lands on god level 6.
# That is the rung that carries the Nightmare grant; Distance Distortion is
# on the 4th-level grant and so is granted on the way up. AddAbilities
# (src/Create.cpp) hands each rung's grants out as the rung is reached.
#
# WHY THE SHEET IS DUMPED PAGE BY PAGE. CreateCharSheet (src/Sheet.cpp) builds
# the whole sheet as one long column and DisplayCharSheet (src/Managers.cpp)
# scrolls it with DOWN; the "Innate Spells" block lives in the Special
# Abilities column, which is below the first screen. Each @dump photographs
# the current scroll position, and DOWN advances it by WinSizeY()-6.
#
# The 's' after the wizard menu buys the one completed turn without which
# tools/headless.sh reports NO GAMEPLAY; entering wizard mode spends none.
# See tools/keys/load-char-sheet.keys for the same one-turn idiom.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Kysul" ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE

# One completed turn (see the header). Searching spends a turn without moving.
s

d
@dump:s0
DOWN
@dump:s1
DOWN
@dump:s2
DOWN
@dump:s3
DOWN
@dump:s4
DOWN
@dump:s5
DOWN
@dump:s6

@quit
